WEBVTT

NOTE Warm Lulu narration; speech-timed captions with scene pauses. Human listening review pending.

1
00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:01.740
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

2
00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:06.559
In this lesson, we will automate a
repeatable task with visible outcomes.

3
00:00:07.019 --> 00:00:11.289
Manual copying between systems costs time
and hides failures when there

4
00:00:11.289 --> 00:00:13.350
is no recorded execution history.

5
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.819
We will explain the features, the setup
decisions, and a

6
00:00:16.819 --> 00:00:18.719
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:23.779
A workflow posts new calls to a team
channel, and a custom field records

8
00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:25.560
the fire district on each call.

9
00:00:25.989 --> 00:00:29.239
Automate repeated administrative steps and
connect Resgrid

10
00:00:29.239 --> 00:00:30.830
to the other systems you use.

11
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.699
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:34.699 --> 00:00:36.930
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:38.309
Workflows.

14
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.079
Automations triggered by department
events.

15
00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:45.529
Start with one workflow for a task you
repeat, and review its runs.

16
00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:47.780
User-defined fields.

17
00:00:48.199 --> 00:00:51.599
Custom fields on calls, personnel and
other records.

18
00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:54.370
Add only the fields you must capture.

19
00:00:55.039 --> 00:00:57.410
API and MCP integrations.

20
00:00:58.109 --> 00:01:01.400
API and MCP access for other systems.

21
00:01:01.809 --> 00:01:05.819
Create credentials for each integration
and limit what they can access.

22
00:01:06.439 --> 00:01:07.280
New Workflow.

23
00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.489
Create an automation workflow.

24
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.870
Have the destination systems and
credentials ready, and

25
00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:15.000
decide who owns each automation.

26
00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:16.799
Workflow Runs.

27
00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.250
The history of workflow runs, including
failures.

28
00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:23.560
Have the destination systems and
credentials ready, and

29
00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.649
decide who owns each automation.

30
00:01:26.309 --> 00:01:28.090
Import and migration planning.

31
00:01:28.569 --> 00:01:31.659
Plan moving your data from another system
into Resgrid.

32
00:01:32.079 --> 00:01:35.129
Have the destination systems and
credentials ready, and

33
00:01:35.129 --> 00:01:37.290
decide who owns each automation.

34
00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:40.869
For the training scenario, work in this
order.

35
00:01:41.389 --> 00:01:41.949
Step 1.

36
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:45.940
Choose one event and an approved
destination for a workflow.

37
00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:47.050
Step 2.

38
00:01:47.569 --> 00:01:51.739
Configure the workflow action, data
mapping, and integration access.

39
00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:52.909
Step 3.

40
00:01:53.329 --> 00:01:57.979
Trigger a controlled demo event and review
Workflow Runs for success or failure.

41
00:01:58.639 --> 00:02:00.149
Now verify the result.

42
00:02:00.509 --> 00:02:04.820
Confirm the intended action at the
destination and inspect the recorded run.

43
00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:08.689
Test a controlled failure and document who
owns retries.

44
00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:13.309
A common problem to watch for: A saved
workflow is not evidence

45
00:02:13.309 --> 00:02:15.249
that its destination received data.

46
00:02:15.579 --> 00:02:19.159
Protected content requires the separately
reviewed egress path.

47
00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.320
Your practice task is simple.

48
00:02:21.779 --> 00:02:25.480
Create a demo-only new-call workflow and
inspect its run.

49
00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:30.830
Record successful and failed execution
evidence, owner, and recovery steps.

50
00:02:31.229 --> 00:02:35.149
Record the result, who owns the follow-up,
and when it should be reviewed.

51
00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:39.029
Use the linked feature scripts for the
detailed screen recording plan.

